  "notes": "USAGE:\nHas both everyday and specialized financial meanings. In tax and accounting contexts, {繰|く}り{戻|もど}す refers to carrying back losses to offset previous years' profits.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {損失|そんしつ}を{繰|く}り{戻|もど}す (to carry back a loss)\n- {時間|じかん}を{繰|く}り{戻|もど}す (to turn back time)\n- {繰戻還付|くりもどしかんぷ} (loss carryback refund)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {繰|く}り{越|こ}す: to carry forward (to future periods)",
